sentences.t:
fas mihi Graiorum sacrata resolvere iura,
fas odisse viros, atque omnia ferre sub auras,
si qua tegunt;

sentences.l:
right for me the Greeks' sacred bonds to loose,
right to hate the men, and everything to bring beneath the breezes,
if they conceal any;

sentences.t:
Nam si vestra manus violasset dona Minervae,
tum magnum exitium (quod di prius omen in ipsum
convertant!) Priami imperio Phrygibusque futurum;

sentences.l:
For if your hand had violated the gifts of Minerva,
then great destruction (which may the gods rather this omen on himself
turn!) for Priam's empire and the Phrygians would be to come;
